      "text": "Johnny has 7 different colored marbles to choose from. To find the number of ways he can choose three different marbles, we can use the combination formula.\n\nThe formula for combinations is:\n\nC(n, r) = n! / (r!(n-r)!)\n\nwhere n is the total number of items, r is the number of items to choose, and ! means the factorial function (for example, 5! = 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1).\n\nIn this case, n = 7 and r = 3.\n\nC(7, 3) = 7! / (3!(7-3)!)\nC(7, 3) = 7! / (3!4!)\nC(7, 3) = (7 × 6 × 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1) / ((3 × 2 × 1)(4 × 3 × 2 × 1))\nC(7, 3) = (7 × 6 × 5) / (3 × 2 × 1)\nC(7, 3) = 210 / 6\nC(7, 3) = 35\n\nTherefore, Johnny can choose 3 different marbles from his bag in 35 ways.\nThe answer is: 35",
